From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:27:19 -0500
Subject: feat: child tabs, the rest

With "Show tabs under the tab that opened them" on: Back at a child's first
page shows its parent and closes the child, which Shift-Cmd-T brings back.
Close Other Tabs keeps the children of the tab it is asked on. A parent's
children fold away under it, from the tab menu or the command bar, and the
row counts them; a press on the count, Unfold Child Tabs or closing the parent
shows them again. What is on screen keeps its row, as under a collapsed folder,
and the fold survives a restart.

A row's clip follows its indent: it was set only when the row's bounds
changed, so a parent pinned left its children's favicons cut at the old
indent (tabs R57).

Why: the rest of S-92 (tabs R60).

Removable when: child tabs go.
